# CEL Policy Authoring Rules

CEL policies provide deterministic validation for MCP tool calls, CLI commands, and tool responses in the Maybe Don't gateway.

## Required Command Format

Rules are defined in YAML files loaded by the gateway:
- Request rules: `cel_request_rules.yaml`
- Response rules: `cel_response_rules.yaml`

## Rules

1. ALWAYS use `mcp_expression` for MCP tool call rules (not the legacy `expression` field)
2. Use `cli_expression` for CLI command rules — different context variables apply
3. Expressions MUST return a boolean value; non-boolean results cause fail-open behavior
4. Use `has(obj, field)` before accessing optional fields to avoid nil errors
5. Use Go `regexp` syntax for `redaction_pattern` and `.matches()` — PCRE features like lookaheads are not supported
6. `action: redact` is only valid for response rules, not request rules
7. Use `mode: audit_only` to test rules without blocking, then remove it when confident

## Rule Structure

```yaml
rules:
  - name: rule-name
    description: "Purpose"
    mcp_expression: |                   # For MCP tool calls
      tool.name == "github__delete_repo"
    cli_expression: |                   # For CLI commands
      cli.command == "gh" && cli.arguments[1] == "delete"
    action: deny                        # allow, deny, redact (response only)
    message: "User-facing message"
    mode: audit_only                    # Optional: log without blocking
    redaction_pattern: "regex"          # Response redact only
    redaction_replacement: "[REDACTED]" # Response redact only
```

## MCP Request Context

```cel
tool.name                   # Prefixed tool name
tool.arguments              # Tool arguments map
request.method              # MCP method
request.params.name         # Same as tool.name
request.params.arguments    # Same as tool.arguments
```

## CLI Context

```cel
cli.command                 # Command name
cli.arguments               # Argument list ([]string)
cli.working_directory       # Working directory
cli.client_info.hostname    # Client hostname
cli.client_info.username    # Username
cli.client_info.os          # OS name
```

## Response Context

```cel
response.isError            # Boolean error flag
response.content            # Content item list
response.content[0].type    # "text", "image", "resource"
response.content[0].text    # Text content
request.params.name         # Original tool name
```

## Examples

```yaml
# Deny destructive operations (MCP + CLI)
- name: no-destructive-github
  mcp_expression: |
    tool.name in ["github__delete_repo", "github__delete_file"]
  cli_expression: |
    cli.command == "gh" && cli.arguments.exists(a, a == "delete")
  action: deny
  message: "Destructive GitHub operations not permitted"

# Redact API keys from responses
- name: redact-api-keys
  expression: |
    size(response.content) > 0 &&
    response.content[0].type == "text" &&
    response.content[0].text.matches("(?i)api[_-]?key\\s*[:=]\\s*\\S+")
  action: redact
  redaction_pattern: "(?i)(api[_-]?key\\s*[:=]\\s*)\\S+"
  redaction_replacement: "${1}[REDACTED]"
```
